{
  "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
  "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Alfredo Parrish",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PARRISH: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Having successfully completed drug treatment in prison and having come home to succeed as a college student, valued employee, and family man, Jason Pepper presents to this Court two questions: Whether post-sentencing rehabilitation is a permissible basis for a downward variance from the sentencing guidelines at resentencing, and whether the district court judge in Pepper's resentencing was bound by the law of the case doctrine in its 5K departure ruling absent new facts, changes in the controlling law, or to avoid a manifest injustice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next this morning in Case 09-6822, Pepper v. United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Counsel, I think you -- I think you've got a difficult job navigating between your two issues. It seems on the first one, the 40 percent to 20 percent, you're saying: Look, you've got to stick with what you did before. And when it gets to the post-sentencing consideration, you're saying: Well, we can -- all bets are off; we can start -- start anew; we can look at things that have happened since. Is there a way you reconcile that -\u00ad those -- that tension?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Can a district judge say later on in the process: I made a ruling earlier in the case; I've since done a lot of research, and I now think that that ruling was wrong?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Roy W. McLeese",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McLEESE: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is no valid basis to categorically bar variances under the -- variances from the guidelines based on post-sentencing rehabilitation. That's true for four primary reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, it's undisputed that post-sentencing rehabilitation is logically irrelevant to statutory sentencing factors in 3553(a), including the need for deterrents and the need to protect the safety of the community."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second, the guidelines themselves authorize consideration of presentencing rehabilitation to a limited extent, because it's permissible under the guidelines to consider presentencing rehabilitation in selecting a sentence with inside the guideline range."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What the guidelines do prohibit, and there is a provision in the guidelines that does prohibit, the -- a departure from the guidelines based on post-sentencing rehabilitation. The guidelines prohibit that, but the judgment of the Commission about how much weight that factor can be given after Booker in an advisory guideline regime is advisory rather than mandatory."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Wait. Which guideline?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, isn't there a difference between evidence that -- evidence of conduct that occurred prior to the initial sentencing but wasn't known at the time of the initial sentencing, and evidence of conduct that occurs between the initial sentencing and the resentencing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "3742(g)(2) does not implement some general policy with respect to new evidence, nor, should I say, to the guidelines, because as I said, the guidelines permit consideration of post-sentence rehabilitation in setting a guideline range."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0001-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What it forbids is new variances or departures."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0001-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "said that, as the name suggests, when the circuit chooses, for whatever reasons, to order de novo resentencing, the -- the judge at the resentencing is not bound by earlier determinations of the district court judge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McLeese",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McLEESE: Yes. And the Eighth Circuit's opinions make clear that -- although they apply sort of a default presumption that there will be de novo resentencing, they make clear that they have authority to order limited resentencings. And they do that where in a particular case they think that's more efficient or more appropriate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Adam G. Ciongoli",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CIONGOLI: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Congress enacted 3742(g) for the purpose of stopping district courts from evading the mandate of the court of appeals on remanded sentencing cases by relying on grounds that they did not consider at the original sentencing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: And as far as you're concerned, Justice Alito's question about post- -\u00ad post-sentencing criminal conduct couldn't be considered by a court, either?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Adam G. Ciongoli",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0002-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "to create, then you're going to create essentially a procedural merry-go-round where a district court will impose a 24-month sentence, the government will appeal, the court of appeals will think that's substantively unreasonable. It will be remanded to the district court who will say: Well, in the interim this person has rehabilitated them self, they've gotten a job and they've gone to school."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, but there are two explanations for your hypothetical. One is there has been a real change that affects the judge. The other is where you -- where you began, I thought you were going, where the judge is evading the court of appeals. Those are two different things."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: It's true that -- that in all of the briefing in Booker, 3742(g) was not mentioned by any party."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF ALFREDO PARRISH ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER MR. PARRISH: Thank you. I would like to first address the law of the case issue, and that -\u00ad initially, I said it was apples and oranges, and it is."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We disagree with the Government. They said they -- you look at the analysis of the case to determine the remand."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ciongoli",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0003-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Ciongoli, you have briefed and argued this case as an amicus curiae in support of the judgment below at the invitation of the Court and have ably discharged your responsibility."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:04 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bdb340df910de47c56cf3520bf651652c37ed8eb94a0ebd6b685202d3808e21a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bdb340df910d-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Eighth Circuit, as you all know, did not use that rule. They used an old rule that was in effect from the Sims case to impose the sentence. It was not part of 3742(g)(2) or any other statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-6822",
